{"name":"Track CMA merger case timelines in Google Sheets and send email reports","nodes":[{"id":"ba214d3b-45c2-4a21-85ec-7ec68eb0923e","name":"Start Here - Overview and Setup","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[-1000,0],"parameters":{"color":1,"width":880,"height":1240,"content":"## Track CMA case timelines with Google Sheets and email\n\n### How it works\nFetches official GOV.UK case data, extracts dated updates and documents, and upserts timeline rows into Google Sheets. Builds one email summary and a complete HTML timeline attachment. Failed cases remain visible in status rows and the report.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Create a Google Sheet with a **Timeline** tab and the exact headers in the setup note below.\n2. Open **Set Email and Sheet Config**: set the spreadsheet ID, tab name, sender and recipient. Edit the sample case paths.\n3. Connect your Google Sheets credential to **Upsert Sheets Timeline Rows**.\n4. Run manually. Check the sheet, source links, case status rows and the HTML attachment in **Format Timeline as HTML**.\n5. Connect SMTP credentials and enable **Email Timeline Digest** only when ready to send.\n6. Set the workflow timezone and activate/publish for weekday 08:00 runs. Default: Europe/London.\n\n### Customization\nAdd CMA case paths, change the schedule, adjust parsing rules or change the report styling. Two historical cases are included as examples.\n\n### Requirements\nGoogle Sheets access; SMTP only for email delivery. Public GOV.UK requests need no API key. Uses built-in nodes, no AI model or other workflow.\n\nThis template covers CMA case pages only. Planned dates remain marked as planned. Check the official source when using a reported deadline."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"95c36166-76ba-4992-a34c-854111c1d9b8","name":"Google Sheets Headers and First Run","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[-1000,1340],"parameters":{"color":4,"width":880,"height":1180,"content":"## Create the Timeline tab\n\nPaste these exact column names into row 1 (one name per column).\n\n`Row Key` · `Case ID` · `Case Name` · `Regulator` · `Sector` · `Parties` · `Jurisdiction` · `Case Status` · `CMA Case URL` · `Snapshot Date` · `Milestone` · `Milestone Date` · `Planned Date` · `Milestone Type` · `Milestone Category` · `Document Title` · `Source Link` · `Parse Status` · `Fetch Error`\n\n**Row Key** is required for upsert. Case ID is the stable GOV.UK page slug, not a legal case-reference number. Parties contains the page description.\n\n### Check your first run\n- Both sample cases should have a status row.\n- Failed/empty cases should be visible as Error or Needs review.\n- Run twice: identical Row Keys should update existing rows.\n- Inspect the HTML attachment before enabling SMTP.\n\n### History and failures\nMilestone rows are retained; removed or changed source content does not delete old sheet rows. The report contains only this run's parsed rows. Stable case-status rows update after recovery.\n\nFetch/parse problems are included in the report. Google Sheets or SMTP failures stop execution and appear in n8n's execution history. Configure a separate error workflow in n8n settings if you need failure notifications."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"38e8b5ba-1496-4c91-a322-12c1e6120e4c","name":"Section 1 - Configure Cases and Schedule","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[0,0],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":920,"height":720,"content":"## 1. Start and configure\n\nStart manually or at 08:00 Monday–Friday in the workflow timezone. Configure the Google Sheet, recipient and case list once.\n\nEach case needs `caseName` and `casePath` such as `/cma-cases/amazon-slash-irobot-merger-inquiry`. The preparation step validates paths, rejects duplicate cases and builds official API URLs."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"622cfe01-74a4-435f-9e30-8b140cc8f44f","name":"Section 2 - Fetch and Extract Dated Events","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[1090,0],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":920,"height":720,"content":"## 2. Fetch and parse cases\n\nRequests are paced one at a time, 500 ms apart. The parser reads GOV.UK `details.metadata`, `details.change_history`, attachments and dated HTML entries.\n\nA status row is emitted for every case, including HTTP errors, malformed responses and pages with no extracted dates. Deadline/expected entries are marked Planned. Repeated identical entries are deduplicated within a case."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"473725d2-8b17-47d6-b910-58234ea0e11e","name":"Section 3 - Store Rows and Build One Report","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[0,850],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":920,"height":680,"content":"## 3. Update sheet and summarize\n\nGoogle Sheets matches on **Row Key**. Identical entries update in place; earlier milestone rows remain available as history.\n\nAfter the write succeeds, the report builder reads all parsed rows from this run, groups them by case and lists review flags. Source text is escaped before it is inserted into HTML."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"be57941e-27e7-4bc0-acdd-900503b6ddb2","name":"Section 4 - Preview and Deliver the Report","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","position":[1090,850],"parameters":{"color":7,"width":920,"height":680,"content":"## 4. Attach and email digest\n\n**Format Timeline as HTML** creates a downloadable `.html` file containing the full timeline. The email uses a compact HTML/plain-text summary and attaches that file; no JavaScript is required.\n\n**Email Timeline Digest is disabled by default.** Connect SMTP, replace the example email addresses in Set Email and Sheet Config, and enable it when ready. Publish/activate the workflow after the manual checks pass."},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"5d71051d-bf03-4a30-a705-f6668bfbb065","name":"Manual Trigger Initiation","type":"n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger","position":[40,270],"parameters":{},"typeVersion":1},{"id":"a4dc4dbf-8075-49bb-b008-359877840771","name":"When Weekday at 8 AM","type":"n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger","position":[40,460],"parameters":{"rule":{"interval":[{"field":"cronExpression","expression":"0 8 * * 1-5"}]}},"typeVersion":1.2},{"id":"2bc9e4bb-1c9f-4f53-aa46-180fd4f32104","name":"Set Email and Sheet Config","type":"n8n-nodes-base.set","position":[310,340],"parameters":{"options":{},"assignments":{"assignments":[{"id":"7bae8b0e-cb9a-40d5-b5ac-cdf409c1d4ba","name":"spreadsheetId","type":"string","value":"YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID"},{"id":"deb69438-e2b3-4d62-8a84-5227a52aef0b","name":"sheetName","type":"string","value":"Timeline"},{"id":"013c7a21-a811-4022-955e-72c635014ab6","name":"senderEmail","type":"string","value":"user@example.com"},{"id":"5aca7a4b-d93a-46f8-9681-69d3214dfcac","name":"recipientEmail","type":"string","value":"user@example.com"},{"id":"ba401b2f-2a36-4f77-998d-ed4842e0fc57","name":"cases","type":"array","value":[{"caseName":"Microsoft / Activision Blizzard","casePath":"/cma-cases/microsoft-slash-activision-blizzard-merger-inquiry"},{"caseName":"Amazon / iRobot","casePath":"/cma-cases/amazon-slash-irobot-merger-inquiry"}]}]}},"typeVersion":3.4},{"id":"f7deaa94-5f20-4631-98ed-f0929b2411ec","name":"Prepare API Case Requests","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[590,340],"parameters":{"jsCode":"const c=$input.first().json;\nif(!Array.isArray(c.cases)||!c.cases.length)throw new Error('Add at least one case in Set Email and Sheet Config.');\nif(!c.spreadsheetId||c.spreadsheetId==='YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID')throw new Error('Set your spreadsheetId in Set Email and Sheet Config, create the Timeline headers, and connect Google Sheets credentials.');\nconst unique=new Set();\nreturn c.cases.map((entry)=>{\n  const path=String(entry.casePath||'').trim().replace(/\\/$/,'');\n  if(!/^\\/cma-cases\\/[a-z0-9-]+$/.test(path))throw new Error('Each casePath must be a GOV.UK /cma-cases/... path.');\n  if(unique.has(path))throw new Error('Duplicate casePath: '+path);unique.add(path);\n  return {json:{caseKey:path.split('/').pop(),caseName:String(entry.caseName||path.split('/').pop()),caseUrl:'https://www.gov.uk'+path,apiUrl:'https://www.gov.uk/api/content'+path}};\n});"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"78372f6b-77c1-4ddc-a37e-e9af92f4e3bc","name":"Fetch GOV UK Case Details","type":"n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest","onError":"continueRegularOutput","position":[1130,340],"parameters":{"url":"={{ $json.apiUrl }}","options":{"timeout":20000,"batching":{"batch":{"batchSize":1,"batchInterval":500}},"response":{"response":{"neverError":true,"fullResponse":true,"responseFormat":"text"}}},"sendHeaders":true,"headerParameters":{"parameters":[{"name":"Accept","value":"application/json"},{"name":"User-Agent","value":"n8n-CMA-Timeline-Template"}]}},"typeVersion":4.2},{"id":"57726b68-552d-43a8-b6c4-5111c6f040d2","name":"Extract Case Milestones","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[1460,340],"parameters":{"jsCode":"// Run once for all items. Keep each response paired to its requested case.\nconst requests = $('Prepare API Case Requests').all();\nconst today = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);\nconst output = [];\nconst decode = s => String(s ?? '').replace(/&#(\\d+);/g, (_, n) => String.fromCodePoint(Math.min(Number(n), 0x10ffff))).replace(/&#x([\\da-f]+);/gi, (_, n) => String.fromCodePoint(Math.min(parseInt(n,16),0x10ffff))).replace(/&nbsp;/gi,' ').replace(/&amp;/gi,'&').replace(/&quot;/gi,'\"').replace(/&#39;|&apos;/gi,\"'\").replace(/&lt;/gi,'<').replace(/&gt;/gi,'>');\nconst clean = s => decode(String(s ?? '').replace(/<script\\b[^>]*>[\\s\\S]*?<\\/script>/gi,' ').replace(/<style\\b[^>]*>[\\s\\S]*?<\\/style>/gi,' ').replace(/<[^>]*>/g,' ')).replace(/\\s+/g,' ').trim();\nconst months = {jan:1,feb:2,mar:3,apr:4,may:5,jun:6,jul:7,aug:8,sep:9,oct:10,nov:11,dec:12};\nfunction dateValue(value) {\n  const text=clean(value); let m,y,mo,d;\n  if ((m=text.match(/\\b(\\d{4})-(\\d{2})-(\\d{2})(?=T|\\b)/))) [,y,mo,d]=m;\n  else if ((m=text.match(/\\b(\\d{1,2})(?:st|nd|rd|th)?\\s+([A-Za-z]+)\\s+(\\d{4})\\b/))) {d=m[1];mo=months[m[2].slice(0,3).toLowerCase()];y=m[3];}\n  else if ((m=text.match(/\\b(\\d{1,2})[./](\\d{1,2})[./](\\d{2}|\\d{4})\\b/))) {d=m[1];mo=m[2];y=m[3].length===2?'20'+m[3]:m[3];}\n  else return '';\n  y=Number(y);mo=Number(mo);d=Number(d);\n  const dt=new Date(Date.UTC(y,mo-1,d));\n  if (!Number.isFinite(dt.getTime())||dt.getUTCFullYear()!==y||dt.getUTCMonth()+1!==mo||dt.getUTCDate()!==d) return '';\n  return `${y}-${String(mo).padStart(2,'0')}-${String(d).padStart(2,'0')}`;\n}\nfunction safeUrl(value, fallback) {\n  const v=decode(value).trim();\n  if (/^https:\\/\\/[^\\s\"<>]+$/i.test(v)) return v;\n  if (/^\\/(?!\\/)/.test(v)) return 'https://www.gov.uk'+v;\n  return fallback;\n}\nfunction hash(text) {let h=2166136261;for(let i=0;i<text.length;i++){h^=text.charCodeAt(i);h=Math.imul(h,16777619);}return (h>>>0).toString(16).padStart(8,'0');}\nfor (let i=0;i<$input.all().length;i++) {\n  const response=$input.all()[i].json;\n  const paired=$input.all()[i].pairedItem;\n  const sourceIndex=Array.isArray(paired)?paired[0]?.item:paired?.item;\n  const context=requests[sourceIndex ?? i]?.json || {};\n  const key=context.caseKey || `unmatched-${i}`;\n  const page=context.caseUrl || '';\n  let base={'Case ID':key,'Case Name':context.caseName||key,'Regulator':'CMA','Sector':'','Parties':'','Jurisdiction':'UK','Case Status':'','CMA Case URL':page,'Snapshot Date':today};\n  const row=(fields)=>({json:{'Row Key':'',...base,'Milestone':'','Milestone Date':'','Planned Date':'','Milestone Type':'','Milestone Category':'','Document Title':'','Source Link':page,'Parse Status':'','Fetch Error':'',...fields},pairedItem:{item:i}});\n  try {\n    if (response.error) throw new Error(typeof response.error==='string'?response.error:(response.error.message||JSON.stringify(response.error)));\n    const status=Number(response.statusCode||200);\n    if (status<200||status>=300) throw new Error(`GOV.UK returned HTTP ${status}`);\n    let data=response.body ?? response.data ?? response;\n    if (typeof data==='string') data=JSON.parse(data);\n    if (!data || typeof data!=='object' || !data.details || !data.title) throw new Error('Response is not a GOV.UK content document');\n    const details=data.details;const meta=details.metadata || data.metadata || {};\n    const pageUrl=safeUrl(data.base_path,page);\n    base={...base,'Case Name':clean(data.title)||base['Case Name'],'Sector':Array.isArray(meta.market_sector)?meta.market_sector.map(clean).join(' / '):clean(meta.market_sector),'Parties':clean(data.description),'Case Status':clean(meta.case_state)||'Unknown','CMA Case URL':pageUrl};\n    const milestones=[];const seen=new Set();\n    function add(date,note,type,category,link,title='') {\n      if (!date||!note) return;\n      note=clean(note);const signature=[date,type,category,note,safeUrl(link,pageUrl)].join('|');\n      if(seen.has(signature)) return;seen.add(signature);\n      milestones.push(row({'Row Key':`${key}|${date}|${hash(signature)}`,'Milestone':note,'Milestone Date':type==='Actual'?date:'','Planned Date':type==='Planned'?date:'','Milestone Type':type,'Milestone Category':category,'Document Title':clean(title),'Source Link':safeUrl(link,pageUrl),'Parse Status':'Live'}));\n    }\n    for(const h of (details.change_history || data.change_history || [])) add(dateValue(h.public_timestamp),h.note,'Actual','Page update',pageUrl);\n    for(const a of (details.attachments || [])) add(dateValue(a.created_at),`Document published: ${clean(a.title)}`,'Actual','Publication',a.url,a.title);\n    const body=typeof details.body==='string'?details.body:'';\n    for(const tr of body.matchAll(/<tr\\b[^>]*>([\\s\\S]*?)<\\/tr>/gi)) {\n      const cells=[...tr[1].matchAll(/<t[dh]\\b[^>]*>([\\s\\S]*?)<\\/t[dh]>/gi)].map(m=>clean(m[1]));\n      if(cells.length<2) continue;\n      const date=cells.map(dateValue).find(Boolean);const text=cells.join(' — ');\n      // A deadline remains planned even after it passes; it is not proof of completion.\n      const planned=/deadline|expected|anticipated|provisional|target|due\\b|planned|by\\b/i.test(text) || date>today;\n      const url=tr[1].match(/href=[\"']([^\"']+)[\"']/i)?.[1] || pageUrl;\n      add(date,text,planned?'Planned':'Actual','Timetable',url);\n    }\n    for(const p of body.matchAll(/<(?:p|li)\\b[^>]*>([\\s\\S]*?)<\\/(?:p|li)>/gi)) {\n      const text=clean(p[1]);\n      const start=text.match(/^(\\d{1,2}(?:st|nd|rd|th)?\\s+[A-Za-z]+\\s+\\d{4})\\s*[:–—-]\\s*(.+)$/);\n      if(!start)continue;\n      const date=dateValue(start[1]);const planned=/expected|anticipated|provisional|planned|will\\b|deadline/i.test(start[2]) || date>today;\n      add(date,start[2],planned?'Planned':'Actual','Dated update',p[1].match(/href=[\"']([^\"']+)[\"']/i)?.[1] || pageUrl);\n    }\n    // A stable status row makes failures visible and gets overwritten on recovery.\n    output.push(row({'Row Key':`${key}|status`,'Milestone':milestones.length?'Case fetch and parse succeeded':'No dated milestones extracted; review source page','Milestone Type':'Status','Milestone Category':'Case status','Parse Status':milestones.length?'Live':'Needs review','Source Link':pageUrl}));\n    output.push(...milestones);\n  } catch(error) {\n    output.push(row({'Row Key':`${key}|status`,'Milestone':'Case fetch or parse failed; review source page','Milestone Type':'Status','Milestone Category':'Case status','Parse Status':'Error','Fetch Error':String(error.message||error).slice(0,500)}));\n  }\n}\nreturn output;\n"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"008d87fb-e57d-4d23-877a-0d9f49ea4bba","name":"Upsert Sheets Timeline Rows","type":"n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets","notes":"Connect your Google Sheets credential. Create the Timeline tab using the exact headers listed in the setup note. Row Key must remain the matching column.","position":[40,1140],"parameters":{"columns":{"value":{},"schema":[{"id":"Row Key","type":"string","display":true,"removed":false,"required":false,"displayName":"Row Key","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Case ID","type":"string","display":true,"removed":false,"required":false,"displayName":"Case ID","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Case Name","type":"string","display":true,"removed":false,"required":false,"displayName":"Case Name","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Regulator","type":"string","display":true,"removed":false,"required":false,"displayName":"Regulator","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Sector","type":"string","display":true,"removed":false,"required":false,"displayName":"Sector","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Parties","type":"string","display":true,"removed":false,"required":false,"displayName":"Parties","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Jurisdiction","type":"string","display":true,"removed":false,"required":false,"displayName":"Jurisdiction","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Case Status","type":"string","display":true,"removed":false,"required":false,"displayName":"Case Status","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"CMA Case URL","type":"string","display":true,"removed":false,"required":false,"displayName":"CMA Case URL","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Snapshot Date","type":"string","display":true,"removed":false,"required":false,"displayName":"Snapshot Date","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Milestone","type":"string","display":true,"removed":false,"required":false,"displayName":"Milestone","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Milestone Date","type":"string","display":true,"removed":false,"required":false,"displayName":"Milestone Date","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Planned Date","type":"string","display":true,"removed":false,"required":false,"displayName":"Planned Date","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Milestone Type","type":"string","display":true,"removed":false,"required":false,"displayName":"Milestone Type","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Milestone Category","type":"string","display":true,"removed":false,"required":false,"displayName":"Milestone Category","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Document Title","type":"string","display":true,"removed":false,"required":false,"displayName":"Document Title","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Source Link","type":"string","display":true,"removed":false,"required":false,"displayName":"Source Link","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Parse Status","type":"string","display":true,"removed":false,"required":false,"displayName":"Parse Status","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true},{"id":"Fetch Error","type":"string","display":true,"removed":false,"required":false,"displayName":"Fetch Error","defaultMatch":false,"canBeUsedToMatch":true}],"mappingMode":"autoMapInputData","matchingColumns":["Row Key"],"attemptToConvertTypes":false,"convertFieldsToString":true},"options":{},"operation":"appendOrUpdate","sheetName":{"__rl":true,"mode":"name","value":"={{ $('Set Email and Sheet Config').first().json.sheetName }}"},"documentId":{"__rl":true,"mode":"id","value":"={{ $('Set Email and Sheet Config').first().json.spreadsheetId }}"}},"typeVersion":4.5},{"id":"279ba579-dd79-4da0-ac3f-d8b65683bf10","name":"Build Timeline Summary Report","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[370,1140],"parameters":{"jsCode":"// Always build one report from the current run's parsed rows, after Sheets succeeds.\nconst rows=$('Extract Case Milestones').all().map(item=>item.json);\nconst config=$('Set Email and Sheet Config').first().json;\nconst esc=v=>String(v??'').replace(/[&<>\"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','\"':'&quot;',\"'\":'&#39;'}[c]));\nconst safeLink=v=>/^https:\\/\\/[^\\s\"<>]+$/i.test(String(v||''))?String(v):'';\nconst cases=new Map();\nfor(const r of rows){const key=r['Case ID'];if(!cases.has(key))cases.set(key,{id:key,name:r['Case Name'],status:r['Case Status'],url:r['CMA Case URL'],rows:[],review:false,error:''});const c=cases.get(key);if(r['Milestone Type']==='Status'){c.review=r['Parse Status']!=='Live';c.error=r['Fetch Error']|| (c.review?r.Milestone:'');}else c.rows.push(r);}\nfor(const c of cases.values())c.rows.sort((a,b)=>String(a['Milestone Date']||a['Planned Date']).localeCompare(String(b['Milestone Date']||b['Planned Date'])));\nconst all=[...cases.values()];const totalMilestones=all.reduce((sum,c)=>sum+c.rows.length,0);const flaggedCases=all.filter(c=>c.review).length;const reportDate=new Date().toISOString().slice(0,10);\nconst tableStyle='border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font:14px Arial,sans-serif';\nconst td='padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #dce3ea;text-align:left;vertical-align:top';\nconst caseHtml=c=>`<section style=\"margin:24px 0\"><h2 style=\"font-size:20px;color:#17324d\">${esc(c.name)}</h2><p>Status: ${esc(c.status||'Unknown')} · ${c.rows.length} extracted milestones${safeLink(c.url)?` · <a href=\"${esc(c.url)}\">Official source</a>`:''}</p>${c.review?`<p style=\"padding:12px;background:#fff1e5;color:#842d0a\">Review required: ${esc(c.error)}</p>`:''}<table style=\"${tableStyle}\"><thead><tr><th style=\"${td}\">Date</th><th style=\"${td}\">Type</th><th style=\"${td}\">Milestone</th></tr></thead><tbody>${c.rows.map(r=>`<tr><td style=\"${td};white-space:nowrap\">${esc(r['Milestone Date']||r['Planned Date']||'—')}</td><td style=\"${td}\">${esc(r['Milestone Type'])}<br><small>${esc(r['Milestone Category'])}</small></td><td style=\"${td}\">${esc(r.Milestone)}${safeLink(r['Source Link'])?`<br><a href=\"${esc(r['Source Link'])}\">Source</a>`:''}</td></tr>`).join('')||`<tr><td colspan=\"3\" style=\"${td}\">No dated milestones extracted in this run.</td></tr>`}</tbody></table></section>`;\nconst note='This report extracts dates from public case pages. Check the linked source for current status and deadlines. A planned date is not evidence that an event occurred.';\nconst summary=all.map(c=>`<tr><td style=\"${td}\">${safeLink(c.url)?`<a href=\"${esc(c.url)}\">${esc(c.name)}</a>`:esc(c.name)}</td><td style=\"${td}\">${esc(c.status||'Unknown')}</td><td style=\"${td}\">${c.rows.length}</td><td style=\"${td}\">${c.review?'Review required':'Parsed'}</td></tr>`).join('');\nconst heading=`CMA case timeline — ${reportDate}`;\nconst emailHtml=`<div style=\"font:15px Arial,sans-serif;max-width:850px;margin:auto;color:#203448\"><h1 style=\"font-size:25px\">${esc(heading)}</h1><p>${all.length} cases · ${totalMilestones} milestones · ${flaggedCases} requiring review</p><table style=\"${tableStyle}\"><tr><th style=\"${td}\">Case</th><th style=\"${td}\">Status</th><th style=\"${td}\">Milestones</th><th style=\"${td}\">Result</th></tr>${summary}</table><p>The complete timeline is attached as an HTML file.</p>${flaggedCases?'<ul>'+all.filter(c=>c.review).map(c=>`<li>${esc(c.name)}: ${esc(c.error)}</li>`).join('')+'</ul>':''}<p style=\"font-size:12px;color:#526679\">${esc(note)}</p></div>`;\nconst timelineHtml=`<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"><title>${esc(heading)}</title></head><body style=\"background:#f3f6fa;font:15px Arial,sans-serif;color:#203448;padding:24px\"><main style=\"max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:32px;background:white\"><h1>${esc(heading)}</h1><p>${all.length} cases · ${totalMilestones} milestones · ${flaggedCases} requiring review</p>${all.map(caseHtml).join('')}<footer style=\"font-size:12px;color:#526679\">${esc(note)}</footer></main></body></html>`;\nreturn [{json:{reportDate,totalCases:all.length,totalMilestones,flaggedCases,emailSubject:`CMA Timeline — ${reportDate} | ${all.length} cases | ${flaggedCases} for review`,emailText:`${heading}\\n${all.length} cases; ${totalMilestones} milestones; ${flaggedCases} require review.\\n\\n${all.map(c=>`${c.name}: ${c.rows.length} milestones, ${c.review?'REVIEW: '+c.error:'parsed'}\\n${c.url}`).join('\\n\\n')}\\n\\nFull report attached. ${note}`,emailHtml,timelineHtml,htmlFileName:`cma-timeline-${reportDate}.html`,senderEmail:config.senderEmail,recipientEmail:config.recipientEmail}}];\n"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"07ec1d25-b84a-4e71-b476-db98d08dda3a","name":"Format Timeline as HTML","type":"n8n-nodes-base.code","position":[1130,1140],"parameters":{"jsCode":"const item=$input.first();\nconst timeline=await this.helpers.prepareBinaryData(Buffer.from(item.json.timelineHtml,'utf8'),item.json.htmlFileName,'text/html');\nreturn [{json:item.json,binary:{timeline}}];"},"typeVersion":2},{"id":"4f34294b-fffa-453c-8b34-3c3f0b02c1cf","name":"Email Timeline Digest","type":"n8n-nodes-base.emailSend","notes":"Disabled for initial preview. Configure senderEmail and recipientEmail, connect SMTP credentials, then enable this node when you want delivery.","disabled":true,"position":[1460,1140],"parameters":{"html":"={{ $json.emailHtml }}","text":"={{ $json.emailText }}","options":{"attachments":"timeline","appendAttribution":false},"subject":"={{ $json.emailSubject }}","toEmail":"={{ $json.recipientEmail }}","fromEmail":"={{ $json.senderEmail }}","emailFormat":"both"},"typeVersion":2.1}],"active":false,"pinData":{},"settings":{"timezone":"Europe/London","executionOrder":"v1"},"connections":{"When Weekday at 8 AM":{"main":[[{"node":"Set Email and Sheet Config","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Extract Case Milestones":{"main":[[{"node":"Upsert Sheets Timeline Rows","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Format Timeline as HTML":{"main":[[{"node":"Email Timeline Digest","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Fetch GOV UK Case Details":{"main":[[{"node":"Extract Case Milestones","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Manual Trigger Initiation":{"main":[[{"node":"Set Email and Sheet Config","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Prepare API Case Requests":{"main":[[{"node":"Fetch GOV UK Case Details","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Set Email and Sheet Config":{"main":[[{"node":"Prepare API Case Requests","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Upsert Sheets Timeline Rows":{"main":[[{"node":"Build Timeline Summary Report","type":"main","index":0}]]},"Build Timeline Summary Report":{"main":[[{"node":"Format Timeline as HTML","type":"main","index":0}]]}}}